the biggest thing for me was that i was  very good at the candidate side i think  it's again it's like a bit of a myth  like a lot of people come into the  industry and of course you know clients  are hugely important like you have to  have clients but i found myself to like  if i was candidate led and candidate  focused then the clients would also come  and they'd be happy as well you can have  all the clients in the world but if you  can't deliver on that candidate side  then  it's not going to work and i think what  i did very well was where i believed  that i really understood what the  candidates wanted i would have really  in-depth conversations with each  candidate but i would quickly know in  the first five minutes by asking a few  good questions what really makes this  candidate tick if this candidate they  have all the skills but if this  opportunity that i'm trying to offer  them isn't right for them they're never  going to take it and there's no point  trying to put a square into round hole  you know so that's what i teach for my  team now is you know from the first  phone call like you have to get a really  good idea what the candidate wants what  really makes them tick and it's much  more difficult i think in this day in  our tech market the candidates have so  much choice but yeah i think it was my  focus on the candidate side and really  trying to give them a genuine service  and understanding where i should put my  time that is key if you have loads of  half-hour conversations with candidates  that never really end up anywhere you're  not going to achieve what you want to  achieve by prioritizing okay this  candidate is super invested this  candidate really wants this job i can  control the situational influencer they  should get your time if you have a  candidate who really isn't invested but  maybe the client likes them or they're  really highly skilled like they still  have your time but maybe not so much so  i think time management's really really  crucial and i think another thing in  hindsight i don't think i really knew  this at the time but one thing that made  me stand out to clients i think was they  could trust me i had a very different  approach and i think i was memorable as  well because of my speech perhaps  because of the fact that i could speak  some german to my clients as well and i  would just try different things and i  think a big thing especially when you're  beginning in this job it's so easy to do  what everybody else is doing it's what  makes you memorable that sticks in  someone's mind you need to get a client  to when you call them to go ah it's john  yeah i know you cool you helped me last  time or you gave me some good advice i  think it's being memorable it's really  really really important the recruitment  mentors podcast is proudly sponsored by  vincerie and the award-winning sauce  breaker  [Music]
 

